{"id": "pr180472", "arm": "coupled", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "exit": 0, "seconds": 87.3, "files": ["homeassistant/components/mobile_app/webhook.py", "homeassistant/components/mobile_app/__init__.py", "homeassistant/components/cloud/__init__.py"], "answered": true, "is_error": false, "subtype": "success", "session_id": "f26548ef-b0a8-48f6-b678-2ef0e3b108af", "num_turns": 9, "cost_usd": 0.12929459999999998, "input_tokens": 179885, "output_tokens": 2661, "answer": {"files": [{"path": "homeassistant/components/mobile_app/webhook.py", "lines": "webhook_get_config (about lines 739-745)", "why": "The config response only sends cloudhook_url and remote_ui_url when the cloud has an active subscription, and otherwise omits them. A client that was told to use hooks.nabu.casa is never told to drop it, so the iOS app keeps retrying that URL."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/mobile_app/__init__.py", "lines": "_async_setup_cloudhook (about lines 128-193), including clean_cloudhook and the manage_cloudhook listener", "why": "The stale CONF_CLOUDHOOK_URL cleanup only happens in some branches and depends on the cloud integration's state, so it needs to reliably strip the stored cloudhook URL when the user is no longer logged in to the cloud."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/cloud/__init__.py", "lines": "async_setup (about lines 286-397) and async_setup_entry (about lines 429-442)", "why": "The cloud config entry and its 3 entities stay loaded after the user logs out and removes `cloud:`; the `_on_start` handler is a possible source of the leftover entry, since it starts a system config flow for cloud."}]}, "tool_calls": 7, "verinoda_calls": 0, "graphify_calls": 0, "network": [], "first_tools": ["Grep", "Grep", "Read", "Grep", "Read"], "assist": {"inject": 0, "coupled_notes": 3, "gate": 0, "nudge": 0, "locate_calls": 0, "coupled_calls": 0, "tool_search": 0}}
{"id": "pr180472", "arm": "tool", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "exit": 0, "seconds": 91.4, "files": ["homeassistant/components/cloud/__init__.py", "homeassistant/components/cloud/client.py", "homeassistant/components/cloud/http_api.py", "homeassistant/components/cloud/config_flow.py"], "answered": true, "is_error": false, "subtype": "success", "session_id": "f4c700fe-77fc-4327-864b-16457d516156", "num_turns": 11, "cost_usd": 0.1436894, "input_tokens": 248867, "output_tokens": 2627, "answer": {"files": [{"path": "homeassistant/components/cloud/__init__.py", "lines": "async_setup (_on_start, ~lines 338-349), async_setup_entry / async_unload_entry (429-449)", "why": "The Cloud config entry is created once on login and reloaded on every boot even when cloud/default_config is absent from YAML. It needs a cleanup path, such as removing the entry on logout or not setting it up when the user is logged out and Cloud is not configured."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/cloud/client.py", "lines": "logout_cleanups (~285-300)", "why": "Logout cleanup does not remove the persisted Cloud config entry, so the integration and its entities survive after the account is disconnected."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/cloud/http_api.py", "lines": "CloudLogoutView.post (~329-346)", "why": "The logout handler logs out and fires the logout event but never removes the Cloud config entry."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/cloud/config_flow.py", "lines": "CloudConfigFlow.async_step_system (~14-18)", "why": "The system flow creates the persistent entry unconditionally. This is where the entry lifecycle would be tied to login state."}]}, "tool_calls": 10, "verinoda_calls": 1, "graphify_calls": 0, "network": [], "first_tools": ["mcp__verinoda-live__locate", "Grep", "Bash", "Read", "Grep"], "assist": {"inject": 0, "coupled_notes": 0, "gate": 0, "nudge": 0, "locate_calls": 1, "coupled_calls": 0, "tool_search": 0}}
{"id": "pr180472", "arm": "full", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "exit": 0, "seconds": 52.7, "files": ["homeassistant/components/cloud/__init__.py", "homeassistant/components/cloud/config_flow.py", "homeassistant/components/mobile_app/__init__.py"], "answered": true, "is_error": false, "subtype": "success", "session_id": "fc243cfe-acbb-43f4-bbba-d8117f336084", "num_turns": 9, "cost_usd": 0.11520340000000001, "input_tokens": 175895, "output_tokens": 1785, "answer": {"files": [{"path": "homeassistant/components/cloud/__init__.py", "lines": "async_setup (_on_start / SOURCE_SYSTEM flow init, ~L338-349) and async_setup_entry (~L429)", "why": "The cloud config entry is created by a SOURCE_SYSTEM flow and then persists, so Cloud and its 3 entities load on every boot even when `cloud:` is not configured and the user is logged out; the entry should be removed or not set up in that case."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/cloud/config_flow.py", "lines": "async_step_system (~L15-25)", "why": "It unconditionally creates the persistent system config entry that keeps the integration loaded after the account is disconnected."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/mobile_app/__init__.py", "lines": "_async_setup_cloudhook (~L128-193), manage_cloudhook", "why": "The stored cloudhook_url is only cleaned when the cloud integration is loaded and reports a disconnect or logout, so once cloud is no longer set up the app keeps being told to use the hooks.nabu.casa webhook."}]}, "tool_calls": 8, "verinoda_calls": 1, "graphify_calls": 0, "network": [], "first_tools": ["mcp__verinoda-live__locate", "Grep", "Grep", "Read", "Grep"], "assist": {"inject": 0, "coupled_notes": 2, "gate": 0, "nudge": 0, "locate_calls": 1, "coupled_calls": 0, "tool_search": 0}}
