{"id": "pr173270", "arm": "tool", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "exit": 0, "seconds": 32.1, "files": ["homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/__init__.py", "homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/config_flow.py", "homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/climate.py"], "answered": true, "is_error": false, "subtype": "success", "session_id": "e90e598a-aa85-4058-ac4f-91dbe7902197", "num_turns": 7, "cost_usd": 0.0750484, "input_tokens": 109366, "output_tokens": 1092, "answer": {"files": [{"path": "homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/__init__.py", "lines": "async_setup_entry, lines ~75-118 (address lookup / skip at 99-110)", "why": "Devices are only given a coordinator if a LAN address was previously stored from DHCP discovery, so on a fresh setup every device is skipped (\"no known LAN address yet\") and gets no entities; it needs a fallback to resolve the LAN address (e.g. cloud-provided IP or active probing) instead of relying solely on DHCP."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/config_flow.py", "lines": "async_step_user (line 34) and async_step_dhcp (lines 79-115)", "why": "The flow stores addresses only via DHCP discovery (CONF_ADDRESSES) and never resolves LAN IPs at account login, so devices on the LAN that DHCP didn't report remain unaddressed."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/climate.py", "lines": "async_setup_entry, lines 70-81", "why": "Entities are created only for devices that have coordinators, so unaddressed devices produce no entities; it must be able to add them later when addresses become known."}]}, "tool_calls": 6, "verinoda_calls": 1, "graphify_calls": 0, "network": [], "first_tools": ["mcp__verinoda-live__locate", "Grep", "Read", "Read", "Grep"], "assist": {"inject": 0, "coupled_notes": 0, "gate": 0, "nudge": 0, "locate_calls": 1, "coupled_calls": 0, "tool_search": 0}}
{"id": "pr173270", "arm": "full", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "exit": 0, "seconds": 32.9, "files": ["homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/__init__.py", "homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/config_flow.py", "homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/manifest.json"], "answered": true, "is_error": false, "subtype": "success", "session_id": "18874f3e-14d5-43c1-baaa-31d5ec8107b3", "num_turns": 8, "cost_usd": 0.0932056, "input_tokens": 115200, "output_tokens": 1230, "answer": {"files": [{"path": "homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/__init__.py", "lines": "async_setup_entry, lines ~75-118 (address lookup / skip loop at 99-110)", "why": "Devices with no stored LAN IP are skipped, so no coordinator or entities exist, and the setup relies solely on DHCP discovery to ever supply an address. Devices on other locations or subnets, or ones already on the network when the entry is created, never get one. A fallback is needed, such as a cloud-provided or probed/mDNS address, or a user-entered IP, along with creating entities for unreachable devices."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/config_flow.py", "lines": "async_step_user (34-76) and async_step_dhcp (79-116)", "why": "The flow never resolves LAN addresses: it creates the entry without any IP and depends on 'registered_devices' DHCP matching. That only fires for devices that renew a lease after registration, so already-connected devices are missed. It needs an address-resolution or manual IP step, or a scan of the current network. Discovery and login are also slow."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/mitsubishi_comfort/manifest.json", "lines": "\"dhcp\": [{\"registered_devices\": true}] (line 6)", "why": "The only address-discovery mechanism is the registered_devices DHCP matcher, which cannot find devices that already hold a lease. Another discovery method, or a library bump that supplies the LAN IP, is needed."}]}, "tool_calls": 7, "verinoda_calls": 1, "graphify_calls": 0, "ne