{"id": "pr172657", "arm": "strict", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "exit": 0, "seconds": 149.4, "files": ["homeassistant/components/homewizard/sensor.py", "homeassistant/components/homewizard/__init__.py"], "answered": true, "is_error": false, "subtype": "success", "session_id": "9f004cd5-1974-4da7-bb36-87442f748157", "num_turns": 6, "cost_usd": 0.0750098, "input_tokens": 108661, "output_tokens": 1160, "answer": {"files": [{"path": "homeassistant/components/homewizard/sensor.py", "lines": "async_setup_entry external-devices loop (~L773-785) and HomeWizardExternalSensorEntity.__init__ (~L823-848: _attr_unique_id, DeviceInfo identifiers/serial_number)", "why": "The external device ID from the API is now prefixed (e.g. \"gas_meter_G0123\u2026\"), so the device identifier, unique_id and serial no longer match the old gas meter device and a second, empty device is created; the prefix must be stripped or the old identifier reused."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/homewizard/__init__.py", "lines": "async_setup_entry (~L88 device registry handling)", "why": "Existing devices/entities registered under the old unprefixed identifier need to be migrated or cleaned up so the empty duplicate device is not left behind."}]}, "tool_calls": 5, "verinoda_calls": 0, "graphify_calls": 0, "network": [], "first_tools": ["Grep", "Read", "Grep", "Grep", "StructuredOutput"], "assist": {"inject": 0, "coupled_notes": 1, "gate": 0, "nudge": 0, "locate_calls": 0, "coupled_calls": 0, "tool_search": 0}}
{"id": "pr179239", "arm": "tool", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "exit": 0, "seconds": 94.8, "files": ["homeassistant/components/cover/__init__.py", "homeassistant/components/opengarage/cover.py"], "answered": true, "is_error": false, "subtype": "success", "session_id": "1b1bef0c-7152-441d-8df3-995ab733eb58", "num_turns": 8, "cost_usd": 0.09855, "input_tokens": 145253, "output_tokens": 1882, "answer": {"files": [{"path": "homeassistant/components/cover/__init__.py", "lines": "_get_toggle_function (final fallback, ~lines 433-446) and the _cover_is_last_toggle_direction_open handling in state (~lines 246-251)", "why": "A cover that reports is_closed False with no position falls back to a stale last-direction flag, so toggle picks open on an open door and does nothing; an open, non-moving cover should close."}, {"path": "homeassistant/components/opengarage/cover.py", "lines": "OpenGarageCover: async_open_cover / async_close_cover early returns (~77-78, 86-87) and _update_attr (~94-104); add an async_toggle override", "why": "The integration sets CLOSING itself and never reports OPENING for external opens, so the flag stays stale and the early return in async_open_cover silently swallows the toggle."}]}, "tool_calls": 6, "verinoda_calls": 1, "graphify_calls": 0, "network": [], "first_tools": ["mcp__verinoda-live__locate", "Grep", "Read", "Read", "Read"], "assist": {"inject": 0, "coupled_notes": 0, "gate": 0, "nudge": 0, "locate_calls": 1, "coupled_calls": 0, "tool_search": 0}}
{"id": "pr166748", "arm": "coupled", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "exit": 0, "seconds": 21.9, "files": ["homeassistant/components/history_stats/data.py"], "answered": true, "is_error": false, "subtype": "success", "session_id": "bcdbb5ac-8e94-49c4-9a64-fbac7cf9f1dc", "num_turns": 3, "cost_usd": 0.0566388, "input_tokens": 52071, "output_tokens": 699, "answer": {"files": [{"path": "homeassistant/components/history_stats/data.py", "lines": "HistoryStats.async_update, the `else` branch that replays self._pending_events after `_async_history_from_db` (about lines 135-147); also the cached-path event append (about lines 115-122) and `_pending_events.clear()`", "why": "Pending state-change events are appended after the DB query without checking whether the query already returned them, so an event that is older than the last DB row (for example a restart-time on to off transition) gets re-added out of order. The history can then end on a stale 'on' state, and `_async_compute_seconds_and_changes` keeps counting time while the sensor is off. The fix is to skip events whose last_changed is not newer than the last stored HistoryState, or to dedupe them."}]}, "tool_calls": 2, "verinoda_calls": 0, "graphify_calls": 0, "network": [], "first_tools": ["Bash", "StructuredOutput"], "assist": {"inject": 0, "coupled_notes": 0, "gate": 0, "nudge": 0, "locate_calls": 0, "coupled_calls": 0, "tool_search": 0}}
